  "falsifies_uniform_charge_bound": false,
  "periodic_nonzero_density_lemma": "On a spatial cycle, zero emitted phase-0 E bits force phase-0 O bits to zero by the E recurrence. The O recurrence then forces phase-1 E to zero, and induction around the p temporal phases forces E=O=0. The all-zero four-word state has only itself as a predecessor, so it is unreachable from the prescribed initial state, whose O word is all ones. Thus every finite-period boundary has positive eventual density; this gives no lower bound uniform in p.",
  "claim_limit": "Exact only for periodic free even-right boundary words in the declared period range and for resolved orbits. A finite negative charge prefix does not refute a bound with an unspecified additive constant; only an eventual cycle density below 1/8 does so."
}
